 "description": "Shared test vectors for CPU and memory parsing, canonicalization and per-field resolution, usable by the Go client library (apps/whr/internal/resources) and later by the Elixir control plane. CPU canonical value is integer thousandths of a CPU equivalent; memory is integer bytes (MiB = 1048576, GiB = 1073741824). Grammar: cpu = int [ '.' 1*3DIGIT ]; memory = int ( 'MiB' / 'GiB' ), int = '0' / nonzero *DIGIT, ASCII digits only, case-sensitive units, no whitespace. Rejections are classified by the first matching rule of classification_order. Spellings with equal canonical values share request identity. Resolution is per field: explicit flag, then host profile, else needs-human (unattended) or prompt (interactive); omission never means unlimited.",
 "limits": {
  "max_canonical": 9223372036854775807,
  "mib": 1048576,
  "gib": 1073741824
 },
